Practical Thought About Practical Thought?
• The first helpful notion is that it is usually best to simplify problems by deciding big "no-
brainer" questions first
• The importance of numerical fluency cannot be overemphasized
• Invert, always invert. Many problems cannot be solved thinking forward, you just
approach them by thinking backwards. What must you avoid because you don't want it?
• The best and most practical wisdom is elementary academic wisdom but you must think
in a multidisciplinary manner
• Lollapalooza effects, very big effects, tend to only come from large combinations of
factors
• The best way to avoid envy, recognized by Aristotle, is to plainly deserve the success we
get

